WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.106
Application security matters because software now sits directly in front of customer data, business workflows, and internal systems.

2
00:00:09.106 --> 00:00:19.936
A small weakness in authorization, input handling, configuration, or monitoring can become a path to data exposure, operational disruption, or loss of trust.

3
00:00:19.936 --> 00:00:31.732
Compliance matters because it gives organizations a repeatable way to describe security expectations, assign responsibilities, and prove that safeguards are being managed.

4
00:00:31.732 --> 00:00:39.734
It does not replace engineering judgment, but it helps teams avoid treating security as a set of disconnected tasks.

5
00:00:39.734 --> 00:00:44.425
OWASP is a community-driven source of application security guidance.

6
00:00:44.425 --> 00:00:57.117
The OWASP Top 10 gives teams a shared vocabulary for the most common and consequential web application risk categories, making it easier to prioritize review, testing, and remediation.

7
00:00:57.117 --> 00:01:06.085
NIST SP 800-53 Rev. 5 is a catalog of security and privacy controls used across federal, regulated, and risk-focused environments.

8
00:01:06.085 --> 00:01:18.916
Its control families cover areas such as access control, audit and accountability, configuration management, incident response, risk assessment, system integrity, and system development.

9
00:01:18.916 --> 00:01:27.401
This course pairs each OWASP Top 10 risk with attack examples, practical mitigations, and selected NIST SP 800-53 controls.

10
00:01:27.401 --> 00:01:35.678
The goal is not to claim automatic compliance, but to help technical teams connect vulnerability work to control intent.

11
00:01:35.678 --> 00:01:39.955
Use OWASP categories to organize application risk discussions.

12
00:01:39.955 --> 00:01:46.026
Use NIST controls to connect technical work to governance, evidence, and accountability.

13
00:01:46.026 --> 00:01:50.441
Treat mappings as guidance that still requires local validation.

14
00:01:50.441 --> 00:02:00.098
Selected NIST mappings for this topic include SA-3 - System Development Life Cycle; RA-3 - Risk Assessment; PM-9 - Risk Management Strategy.

